,"created_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:44Z"},{"id":719129704,"node_id":"RA_kwDOPYoUTM4q3Qxo","name":"openspec-windows-x64.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":45093762,"digest":"sha256:6c00846a7e4813366ff8395cef71cadcc11d66eb7a112fe332358f8de5ae230e","download_count":158,"created_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:44Z"},{"id":719129791,"node_id":"RA_kwDOPYoUTM4q3Qy_","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":754,"digest":"sha256:469bfca5caa1cc86802421c0dab803d67b30a0eca81e34bafe8cccfbc73e5885","download_count":484,"created_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T00:53:45Z"}],"body":"## What's New in v1.16.1\n\nA patch release that makes spec validation stricter and more forgiving in the right places, and makes `openspec version --check` reliable.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **Closed section headings** - `validate`, `show`, `list`, `view` and `archive` now read headings with a closing `#` run (`## Purpose ##`, `## ADDED Requirements ##`) the same as their unclosed forms.\n- **Unrecognized delta sections** - `validate` now fails, and `archive` refuses, when a delta spec puts a requirement under an unrecognized section such as `## DEPRECATED Requirements`, instead of passing with a warning and silently dropping that requirement.\n- **Version check with telemetry off** - `openspec version --check` now checks for a newer version even when telemetry is off or it runs in CI. Only `OPENSPEC_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` skips it; the background check in `openspec update` still honors the telemetry opt-out and CI.\n- **Standalone update offers** - `openspec version --check` on the standalone binary now offers only a release whose files are attached on GitHub, the same one `openspec install` would install, rather than a version npm has before the installer can get it.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/compare/v1.16.0...v1.16.1\n","reactions":{"total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}
